# Force a consistent line ending (LF) for all text files, regardless of
# which OS/tool checks them out (Windows GitHub Desktop vs. the Linux
# sandbox used for parts of this project's tooling). Without this, Git's
# per-platform autocrlf behavior flips files between CRLF/LF on checkout,
# which shows up as every file being "modified" with no real content
# change. Android/Gradle/Kotlin tooling doesn't care about LF vs CRLF, so
# standardizing on LF avoids the churn entirely.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Common binary types some check-in soon (icons/keystores/fonts) - never
# text-normalize these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
